[% META
        title = "Template Documentation"
   description = "Documentation for system templates"
   roles = "admin,developer"
   TemplateType = "Documentation"
   category = "templates"
   page_version = "0.10"
   last_updated = "Sun Aug 09 2026"
   site_specific = "false"
   project_id = "47"
   project_code = "Doc"
%]
[% PageVersion = 'Documentation/DocumentationTtTemplate.tt,v 0.10 2026/08/09 hermes-agent Exp shanta - Self-compliant: no inline CSS; class-based theme styling; RULE reminder added' %]
[% IF c.session.debug_mode == 1 %]
    [% PageVersion %]
[% END %]
[%#
  ============================================================================
  RULE — STYLING FOR AI AUTHORS (read before editing any .tt doc)
  ============================================================================
  NEVER write inline `style="..."` attributes and NEVER hardcode colours
  (hex/rgb). The whole point of the theme system is that themes override
  canonical CSS variables, so inline values silently break every other theme
  and confuse the AI that copies this file.

  Do ONE of these two things, in this order of preference:
    1. USE A THEME-COMPLIANT CLASS. The utility classes defined in the <style>
       block below (.doc-h1, .doc-toc, .doc-navlink, .doc-warning, .doc-table,
       etc.) cover every layout/colour need of a doc page. Prefer these.
    2. IF you must style something not covered by a class, use ONLY a canonical
       var(--name, fallback) — never a literal colour. e.g.
       style="color: var(--text-color);" is the ONLY acceptable inline form,
       and only when no class exists yet.

  Canonical variables live in static/css/base.css. Use only these names:
  --text-color --background-color --primary-color --secondary-color
  --accent-color --link-color --border-color --table-header-bg
  --success-color --warning-color --info-color --caution-color
  --text-muted-color --nav-bg --nav-text --header-font --body-font
  --font-size-small --font-size-large --spacing-small --spacing-medium
  --spacing-large --container-width.

  This template itself contains ZERO inline style= in its body — copy that
  habit. If you add inline style= here, you are teaching the AI the wrong thing.
  ============================================================================
%]
[%#
  DOCUMENTATION SYSTEM STANDARD (S1-S7) — see /Documentation/STANDARD:
  This .tt template REMAINS the live master template (META block, theme classes,
  flat /Documentation/FILENAME links). Categorization/role visibility are owned
  by SQL (documentationmetadataindex). The META title/description/page_version/
  last_updated fields stay as-is.
%]
[%#
  RULE P1 — A PLAN MUST BE LINKED TO A PROJECT.
  A plan with no project is untrackable. No suitable project? CREATE one.
  Phases are SUB-PROJECTS, not single todos. Do not invent numbers:
  GET /api/projects and /api/todos and use real ids.
  META project_id + project_code are required. Pass them into
  _doc_header.tt as doc_project_id / doc_project_code — the shared header
  then renders Open project + View todos at the TOP of every plan so the
  user can jump to tracking without scrolling.
  RULE P2 — EVERY PLAN NEEDS A ROUTINE-UPDATE TODO (recurring re-audit).
  RULE P3 — .tt ONLY, NOT .md.
%]
[%# The .doc-* utility classes (.doc-h1, .doc-toc, .doc-navlink, .doc-warning,
    .doc-table, etc.) live in the SHARED static/css/components/documentation.css
    (loaded by every Documentation page). They are NOT defined here, so this
    template stays 100% inline-style-free and the same classes are reusable by
    every other plan doc. NEVER add a <style> block with inline-styled classes
    here — add shared classes to documentation.css instead. #%]

<div class="container">
    [%# Shared, META-driven page header (title + Open project / View todos +
        site/role/updated + Documentation Home / Suggest Edit). Mirrors the .md
        viewer header so every plan page jumps to its project from the top.
        Data comes from the Documentation controller stash (META project_id).
        See admin/documentation/_doc_header.tt. %]
    [% INCLUDE 'admin/documentation/_doc_header.tt'
        page_title   = 'Documentation Page Title'
        site_name    = site_name
        user_role    = user_role
        last_updated = last_updated
        page_name    = page_name
        doc_project_id   = project_id
        doc_project_code = project_code %]

    <!-- TABLE OF CONTENTS SECTION -->
    <div id="toc" class="row doc-toc">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 class="doc-h2">Quick Navigation</h2>
            <p class="doc-muted">Jump to section:</p>
            <div class="doc-navrow">
                <a href="#overview" class="doc-navlink">Overview</a>
                <a href="#prerequisites" class="doc-navlink">Prerequisites</a>
                <a href="#features" class="doc-navlink">Key Features</a>
                <a href="#getting-started" class="doc-navlink">Getting Started</a>
                <a href="#advanced" class="doc-navlink">Advanced Usage</a>
                <a href="#troubleshooting" class="doc-navlink">Troubleshooting</a>
                <a href="#config-ref" class="doc-navlink">Configuration</a>
                <a href="#project-tracking" class="doc-navlink">Project Tracking</a>
                <a href="#see-also" class="doc-navlink">See Also</a>
            </div>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- OVERVIEW SECTION -->
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="overview" class="doc-h2">1. Overview</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">Brief overview of what this documentation covers. This should be 1-2 sentences explaining the purpose and scope.</p>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- PREREQUISITES & KEY FEATURES SECTION -->
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-50">
            <h2 id="prerequisites" class="doc-h2">2. Prerequisites</h2>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li>Requirement 1</li>
                <li>Requirement 2</li>
                <li>System access level needed</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="col-50">
            <h2 id="features" class="doc-h2">3. Key Features</h2>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><strong>Feature 1</strong>: Description of feature</li>
                <li><strong>Feature 2</strong>: Description of feature</li>
                <li><strong>Feature 3</strong>: Description of feature</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- GETTING STARTED SECTION -->
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="getting-started" class="doc-h2">4. Getting Started</h2>

            <h3 id="gs-step1" class="doc-h3">4.1 Step 1: Initial Setup</h3>
            <p class="doc-body">Detailed instructions for the first step.</p>

            <div class="doc-codebox">
                <pre><code>
# Example code or command
example_command --parameter value
                </code></pre>
            </div>

            <h3 id="gs-step2" class="doc-h3">4.2 Step 2: Configuration</h3>
            <p class="doc-body">Instructions for configuration step.</p>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li>Configure option A</li>
                <li>Set parameter B</li>
                <li>Verify setting C</li>
            </ul>

            <h3 id="gs-step3" class="doc-h3">4.3 Step 3: Verification</h3>
            <p class="doc-body">How to verify everything is working correctly.</p>

            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ADVANCED USAGE SECTION -->
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="advanced" class="doc-h2">5. Advanced Usage</h2>

            <h3 id="adv-feature1" class="doc-h3">5.1 Advanced Feature 1</h3>
            <p class="doc-body">Description and usage instructions for advanced features.</p>

            <h3 id="adv-integration" class="doc-h3">5.2 Integration with Other Systems</h3>
            <p class="doc-body">How this feature integrates with other parts of the application.</p>

            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- TROUBLESHOOTING SECTION -->
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="troubleshooting" class="doc-h2">6. Troubleshooting</h2>

            <div class="doc-warning">
                <h3>Problem: Common Issue 1</h3>
                <p class="doc-body"><strong>Symptoms:</strong> Description of symptoms</p>
                <p class="doc-body"><strong>Solution:</strong> Step by step solution</p>
            </div>

            <div class="doc-info">
                <h3>Problem: Common Issue 2</h3>
                <p class="doc-body"><strong>Symptoms:</strong> Description of symptoms</p>
                <p class="doc-body"><strong>Solution:</strong> Step by step solution</p>
            </div>

            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- CONFIGURATION REFERENCE SECTION -->
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="config-ref" class="doc-h2">7. Configuration Reference</h2>

            <table class="doc-table">
                <tr>
                    <th class="doc-th">Parameter</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">Type</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">Default</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">Description</th>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">parameter_1</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">string</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">"default_value"</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Description of parameter</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td">parameter_2</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">boolean</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">true</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Description of parameter</td>
                </tr>
            </table>

            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- PROJECT TRACKING SECTION (RULE P1 — REQUIRED FOR PLAN DOCUMENTS) -->
    <!-- Delete this whole block for non-plan reference pages. For a PLAN it is mandatory:
         META must also carry project_id and project_code. Use REAL ids from
         GET /api/projects and GET /api/todos — never invent numbers. -->
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="project-tracking" class="doc-h2">Project Tracking</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">
                Owning project:
                <a href="/project/details?project_id=NNN" class="doc-link">#NNN (PROJECT-CODE)</a>
                &mdash; parent: <a href="/project/details?project_id=PPP" class="doc-link">#PPP</a>.
                Each phase below is a <strong>sub-project</strong>, not a single todo.
            </p>
            <table class="doc-table">
                <tr>
                    <th class="doc-th">Phase / Sub-project</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">Tracking item</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">Gate / Done when</th>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">Phase A &mdash; short name</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><a href="/todo/details?record_id=NNNN" class="doc-link">todo NNNN</a></td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Demonstrable condition, not "looks done"</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td">ROUTINE re-audit (RULE P2)</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><a href="/todo/details?record_id=NNNN" class="doc-link">todo NNNN</a> (recurring)</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Keeps this doc from going stale</td>
                </tr>
            </table>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- SEE ALSO SECTION -->
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <div id="see-also" class="doc-success">
                <h2 class="doc-h3">8. See Also</h2>
                <ul class="doc-body">
                    <li><a href="/Documentation/related_doc_1" class="doc-link">Related Documentation 1</a></li>
                    <li><a href="/Documentation/related_doc_2" class="doc-link">Related Documentation 2</a></li>
                    <li><a href="/admin" class="doc-link">Administrative Interface</a></li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- FOOTER SECTION -->
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <div class="doc-footer">
                <p>For technical support or questions about this documentation, contact the system administrator.</p>
                <p><em>This documentation is part of the Comserv system.</em></p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<!--
THEME COMPLIANCE NOTES FOR DEVELOPERS:

This template is fully theme-compliant and SELF-CONTAINED with NO inline styles:

1. **No inline CSS, no hardcoded colours.** Every style is a class in the <style>
   block above (.doc-*), and every class consumes ONLY canonical CSS variables
   (--text-color, --primary-color, --spacing-*, etc. from static/css/base.css).
   Authors copy the classes, never inline style=. This is the rule the AI is
   taught — the template must model it. If you need a style not covered by a
   .doc-* class, ADD the class here; do not fall back to inline style=.

2. **Layout System** (from layout.css): .container / .row / .col-100 / .col-50.

3. **Color-Coded Content Blocks**: .doc-warning (--warning-color), .doc-info
   (--info-color), .doc-success (--success-color) — left-border accent cards.

4. **Responsive Design**: layout.css media queries adapt automatically.

5. **Theme authoring vs template compliance** (two goals):
   - Goal A (authoring): static/config/theme_definitions.json.
   - Goal B (this template): consume canonical var(--*) so pages work on every theme.

6. **Cross-Theme Compatibility**: Default, CSC, USBM, APIS, and any future theme.

7. **Navigation Features**: TOC (id="toc") with quick-jump .doc-navlink chips;
   anchor ids on all sections 1-8; "Back to Top" (.doc-backtop) after each
   major section; self-contained (no relative paths).

8. **DOCUMENTATION LINK FORMAT** (CRITICAL — also in /Documentation/DevelopmentStandards):
   - CORRECT: <a href="/Documentation/FILENAME">Link Text</a>
   - WRONG:   <a href="/Documentation/system/FILENAME.tt">...</a>  (no subdir, no .tt)
   - Flat namespace: strip .tt extension, ignore subdirectories.
   - Non-doc links (admin, todo): full path as-is, e.g. <a href="/admin">Admin</a>

Usage: Replace placeholder content; keep classes + anchors. Add new styles as
.doc-* classes here — never as inline style=. When linking docs, use
/Documentation/FILENAME (no subdir, no .tt).
-->
